cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Study 1 of When Machines Say They Care, please cite this repository release."
type: dataset
title: "When Machines Say They Care: Study 1"
version: "study1-v1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-14
authors:
  - family-names: "Duffy"
    given-names: "Robert Leo"
    affiliation: "Bo Chesterton"
repository-code: "https://github.com/quumble/when-machines-say-they-care"
url: "https://github.com/quumble/when-machines-say-they-care"
abstract: >-
  Study 1 is a controlled API study of relational response language in four
  language-model systems. A fixed 108-prompt factorial battery varied stated
  age, claimed interaction history, non-crisis distress intensity, relational
  bid, and wording frame. The repository preserves the outcome-blind
  preregistration, 1,728 planned raw trials, a 432-response confirmatory Tier 1
  human-coded packet, a nested descriptive/construct-validating Tier 2 review,
  frozen analysis outputs, reviewer-requested post hoc sensitivity analyses,
  technical and human-access papers, and provenance records.
keywords:
  - "language models"
  - "relational AI"
  - "care language"
  - "anthropomorphism"
  - "human support"
  - "preregistration"
